# streams3 — capping a stream with MAXLEN
#
# Learn: XADD key MAXLEN n * ... appends and trims the oldest entries so
# at most n remain. MAXLEN ~ n is the cheap, approximate form: it only
# drops whole internal nodes (100 entries each by default), so the stream
# may keep more than n. Great for "about the last million", useless for
# "exactly the last 3".
#
# Task: append cpu=42 to metrics:host1 and keep EXACTLY the 3 newest
# entries. The check seeds 10 entries first.
#

XADD metrics:host1 MAXLEN ~ 3 * cpu 42
